Z||000005||Two88GTs||10-11-2001||01:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Dumba$$:<BR><B>i was in walmart tonight and came across some bulbs that ive never seen before and they looked the same as the 194's but the  bulb no. is   W5W    the same bulb but 5 watts id suppose?? vs. the 194's that are 3 watts? i just got a pack of 2 (to see if they would work) and put them in the guage pod  WOW!!! their bright, huge diff. ill be going back tomorrow to get some more for the rest of my guages the only thing that sux is there $5 for 2 bulbs<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>An cheaper alternative for 5W bulbs are 2825s used by some European makes(VW for example).<BR>If you follow any late 90s to current year VW at night you'll notice that their license plate lights are REALLY bright.  AutoZone has'em for the same price as 194s(less than $2 for a pair BUT they usually don't have many pairs on the rack)<BR>||||reg||1
